The '''Ginmids'''<ref name="TROS VD" /> were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]].<ref name="Din" /> They were [[Limb|bipedal]] with two five-fingered hands, [[Color|light green]] skin, and a flattened [[nose]] with prominent nostrils. At some point prior to the outbreak of the [[First Order-Resistance War]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> in [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the Ginmid [[Tommet Sozach]] was the [[commander]] of a [[Ginmid mercenary army|mercenary army]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> composed exclusively of Ginmids.<ref name="Din" /> After [[the galaxy]] entered a prolonged period of peace,<ref name="TROS VD" /> the [[army]] was disbanded<ref name="Din" /> and Sozach struck out on his own, making a living as a crowd-pleasing trick shooter.<ref name="TROS VD" />

By [[35 ABY]],<ref name="35 ABY">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' describes the state of [[the galaxy]] up to and during the events of {{Film|IX}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[35 ABY]].</ref> Sozach&mdash;who had by then become a personal defense instructor [[Death penalty|sentenced to death]] after<ref name="TROS VD" /> a [[Death|fatal]] accident in a marksmanship show that he had been putting on<ref name="Din" />&mdash;occasionally felt remorse over giving up the leadership of the Ginmid army,<ref name="TROS VD" /> most of whose [[soldier]]s had become retired.<ref name="Din" /> At one point that [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="35 ABY" /> Sozach was present at the [[Spice Runners' Den]] in [[Kijimi City]] on<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref> the [[Mid Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Kijimi]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Ginmid species first appeared in<ref name="TROS" /> the [[2019]] [[sequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']],<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> where the Ginmid Tommet Sozach was portrayed by [[Phill Woodfine]].<ref name="Woodfine">{{Twitter|username=JakeLuntDavies|url=status/1867512838560047458|name=[[Jake Lunt Davies]]|date=2024-12-13|quote=Tommet Sozach pg136 TROS visual guide. Designed by me. Performed by Phil Woodfine|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/cEmYD|archivefile=File:JakeLuntDavies-SozachActor-Twitter.png}} {{C|In response to: Interesting, I was re-watching the TROS BTS segment "Cast of Creatures," and noticed this individual in the background having what appears to be gray face paint and some wrinkled prosthetics being applied. Can't say I recall seeing this species in anything else?}}</ref> The creature design for Sozach was done by [[Jake Lunt Davies]],<ref name="LuntDavies">{{Twitter|CalumAWatt|status/1273556243261657088|[[Calum Alexander Watt]]|date=2020-06-18|quote=From The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker by @PhilSzostak. Costume concept art for Kijimi crowd, Tommet Sozach 2018. Creature design by Jake Lunt Davies. Alternate options for the same creature.|archivedate=20230224135005}}</ref> and costume concept artist [[Calum Alexander Watt]] created a [[:File:Wizard_14_Version_1A.png|piece of concept art]] of the character.<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref> The species was identified by name in the film's accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

